ing Donald Trump as Speaker of  the House even without him being a  member of the House of Representatives  impeaching Joe Biden and then having  Donald Trump preside over the vote to  impeach Joe Biden in the house  beleaguered radical republican  Congressman Matt Gates is is really into  this idea  starting back in July he started talking  about if we win in 22 we will make  Donald Trump speaker of the house and at  the time it seemed that it might have  just been a publicity ploy to fundraise  get attention maybe raise money for his  legal defense fund but Matt Gates  mentioned it again in August and he  mentioned it again yesterday senior  White House correspondent for Yahoo news  Alexander nazarian published a tweet  about this saying quote Matt Gates just  told me at a press conference that if  Republicans win the house in 22 he will  move to install Trump as house speaker  so there are really three questions here  question one is Matt Gates serious he  appears to be second question would  Republicans actually nominate Trump to  be speaker of the house if they took  control and the third question is if  nominated would Republicans overall  actually vote to make Donald Trump  Speaker of the House the answers to the  first two questions are pretty simple  Matt Gates is serious  and I do think that Donald Trump would  be nominated for speaker of the house if  Republicans take control in 2022 the  third question is the key question  just because Republicans take control  and someone nominates Trump to be  speaker do they really elect Trump to be  Speaker of the House understand that  it's an open question not morally but  strategically if Trump is don't do  particularly well in the November  midterms if Donald Trump's power within  the party seems diminished it's less  likely that Republicans would be willing  to do something so cartoonish on the  other hand and particularly if  Republicans take control of the house on  the basis of many trumpists winning new  sea